###############################################################################

After doing the geometrical design, it uses the time domain solver (home-> setup solver)
In microstrips they use the waveguide port. 
If you select the surface that you want to excite, you can go to
home->vba macros -> solver->ports-> calculate port extension
you got a tool that helps you to compute the size of the waveguide port

In simulation frequency you set the target freq range, idem you can set the 
boundary conditions and the background.

If you want to capture some values you have to add monitors (for example the surface current
or the farfield)
Finally you can modify the setup of the solver there too.

